# ttychatter C changelog

## 0.1.0-c-cli

### Added
- Initial C command-line ttychatter client
- Traditional file-in/file-out workflow: `ttychatter input.txt output.log`
- OpenRouter chat-completions support through libcurl
- JSON request/response handling through json-c
- XDG-style config/cache/data defaults
- Config file loading from `~/.config/ttychatter/config`
- Environment API-key support through `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` and `TTYCHATTER_API_KEY`
- Plaintext API-key setup command
- Optional GPG-encrypted API-key setup command
- API-key forget command
- Doctor diagnostics command
- Model cache update command
- Model listing from cache
- Model search filter
- Model type filter for routers/fixed/free/auto
- Single-model test command
- Input file to output session log workflow
- Session continuation by reusing the same output file
- Context reconstruction from recent output-file turns
- Repeatable `--attach` / `-a` option
- Text attachment insertion
- Image attachment data URL support for compatible models
- Long fenced-code-block extraction into attachment files
- Loopback output mode for piping AI responses to stdout
- Traditional Unix man page
- Step-by-step WALKTHROUGH document
- Verbose maintainer comments in source code

### Notes
- This is not an ncurses client.
- This version intentionally starts with traditional command-line semantics.
- Non-image binary attachments are listed but not fully embedded yet.
- Encrypted API-key storage uses the external `gpg` command rather than linking a crypto library.
